  NodeNumber: 
  Background: {fileID: 0}
  narrativeText: You quietly follow your neighbors in the elevator down to the basement,
    where the parking garage is supposed to be. When the elevator doors open, a wave
    of warm, damp, bloody air hits you. Before you is no longer a parking garage,
    but a deep and winding cavern wrapped in crimson flesh, as though you are inside
    some living creature. The entire cavern rises and falls in a slow pulse. Crawling
    low, you peer inside and see your neighbors deeper within, shoveling chunks of
    flesh from the cave into their buckets. You cannot see clearly, but their faces
    seem to wear satisfied smiles.
